There's no way the higher-ups are going to deal with that.

00:23:20.150 --> 00:23:22.410
Basically, in the current labor system,

00:23:22.850 --> 00:23:24.340
it's impossible for a program to go bankrupt.

00:23:25.240 --> 00:23:27.600
That's what the company and the manufacturer agree on.

00:23:28.440 --> 00:23:29.920
Well, it's...

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:32.220
It's a mistake of the officer's investigation. It's not a man-made accident, it's a kick.

00:23:32.500 --> 00:23:37.560
With the testimony of the doctor and the two-month labor team, the police won't move.

00:23:38.140 --> 00:23:47.460
If it's a loan, it's no good. This is all I have.

00:23:47.840 --> 00:23:51.470
Hey, please collect all the records and reports from this month.

00:23:52.760 --> 00:23:54.250
What are you going to do?

00:23:54.690 --> 00:23:55.690
It's okay. Do it right away.

00:23:56.710 --> 00:23:57.130
Hey!

00:23:57.490 --> 00:23:59.180
Do you have a refrigerator?

00:24:00.480 --> 00:24:01.020
You can use the computer room.

00:24:05.300 --> 00:24:05.780
Hello!

00:24:06.160 --> 00:24:09.910
You're good at using people as usual.

00:24:10.690 --> 00:24:11.750
It's not about people.

00:24:12.210 --> 00:24:13.270
It's about common sense.

00:24:14.110 --> 00:24:16.140
Captain, we got a call from Detective Matsui.

00:24:17.600 --> 00:24:19.300
Oh, send it to the headquarters.

00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:21.350
What did you start?

00:24:21.650 --> 00:24:22.640
You're interested, right?

00:25:52.524 --> 00:25:52.724
Yes.

00:25:53.228 --> 00:25:55.228
Shigeo Shiba from Tokyo City Police.

00:25:56.140 --> 00:25:57.140
Just be sure to be cool.

00:25:58.316 --> 00:25:59.076
Section number two.

00:25:59.692 --> 00:25:59.992
I'm sorry.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:03.250
Oh, yeah. Can't get plenty. Yes.

00:26:14.440 --> 00:26:16.980
Noaka, if you stand there, you'll catch a cold.

00:26:17.280 --> 00:26:18.480
Get some sleep.

00:26:18.780 --> 00:26:19.970
You don't know when you'll be dispatched.

00:26:20.890 --> 00:26:21.350
Yeah.

00:26:22.940 --> 00:26:24.380
You too, Kusuma.

00:26:24.800 --> 00:26:25.040
Yeah.

00:26:46.440 --> 00:26:48.550
It's small, but I didn't have enough to take care of.

00:26:48.970 --> 00:26:50.600
Hiromi-chan, you're really good.

00:26:51.420 --> 00:26:52.180
Everyone will be happy.

00:26:53.120 --> 00:26:54.460
Then, Izumi-san, I'm counting on you.

00:26:54.620 --> 00:26:55.560
It's not like you're going to ship it.

00:26:56.360 --> 00:26:57.320
It's just a red one that's sold out.

00:26:58.330 --> 00:26:58.650
Okay.

00:26:58.950 --> 00:26:59.230
Huh?

00:27:00.060 --> 00:27:02.640
By the way, what's wrong with Asuma? Didn't he say he'd help us?

00:27:03.920 --> 00:27:09.770
He said he'd go to the captain's office, but it looks like he spent the night doing some research yesterday, so I don't think that's the case.

00:27:10.660 --> 00:27:16.690
I wonder if it's okay for him to go to the captain's office?

00:27:17.790 --> 00:27:19.570
A labor manufacturer that caused the crash.

00:27:21.050 --> 00:27:28.790
From the maintenance of the aircraft to the appearance of the crew, we have checked as many items as possible, but there is only one thing that is common with any accident.

00:27:30.600 --> 00:27:34.140
It's a fact that all the laborers that went bankrupt had Shinohara HOS.

00:27:35.860 --> 00:27:39.880
But HOS has more than 80% of all registered laborers.

00:27:40.380 --> 00:27:43.400
But we can't ignore the 100% data.

00:27:44.720 --> 00:27:45.880
And one more thing.

00:27:46.420 --> 00:27:47.340
Two months ago, an outbreak occurred.

00:27:48.780 --> 00:27:50.850
This is exactly the time when HOS was announced.

00:27:52.010 --> 00:27:54.690
With this much data, there's no doubt about it.

00:27:54.730 --> 00:27:56.490
HOS must have a fatal flaw.

00:27:56.490 --> 00:27:56.930
I should have a sense of responsibility.

00:27:57.190 --> 00:27:59.090
I should submit this data to the right person.

00:28:00.380 --> 00:28:02.620
We should announce the program to Shinohara Jukou.

00:28:03.540 --> 00:28:04.020
Captain!

00:28:06.070 --> 00:28:09.600
HOS is a revolutionary OS that Shinohara Jukou made based on the shares.

00:28:11.100 --> 00:28:15.630
If it turns out to be a defective product, it could be fatal.

00:28:16.430 --> 00:28:21.670
Besides, the employees who are responsible for the labor OS are incompetent.

00:28:21.990 --> 00:28:25.960
If there was a bug in HOS, they would have been caught at the debunking stage.

00:28:26.900 --> 00:28:27.840
But...

00:28:27.840 --> 00:28:28.600
Well, listen.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:37.030
As you said, what if the relationship between the host and a series of rampant accidents has been approved, and the host as an OS does not have a defect?

00:28:38.820 --> 00:28:39.180
Huh?

00:28:40.110 --> 00:28:47.840
In other words, what if the rampant accident is not the result of the program bug, but is intentionally programmed?

00:29:00.410 --> 00:29:01.590
Can you read this?

00:29:01.590 --> 00:29:02.460
It's from Matsui-san.

00:29:03.080 --> 00:29:10.190
A report on Aichi Oba.

00:29:10.450 --> 00:29:10.850
Oba?

00:29:10.870 --> 00:29:13.870
Is Oba Aichi that programmer?

00:29:14.330 --> 00:29:15.970
Oba Aichi.

00:29:16.290 --> 00:29:18.750
A software developer from Shinohara High School.

00:29:18.870 --> 00:29:21.180
He was a genius programmer who developed his own software.

00:29:23.870 --> 00:29:26.260
He's 30 years old.

00:29:26.380 --> 00:29:28.320
He's been studying at MIT for 97 years.

00:29:29.110 --> 00:29:29.760
He's just...

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:30.380
He's a Shinnohara resident.

00:29:30.920 --> 00:29:33.400
He has no name, no history, no gender.

00:29:33.920 --> 00:29:36.100
He's about 170cm tall.

00:29:36.160 --> 00:29:39.550
He has no other physical features, including his medical history.

00:29:39.550 --> 00:29:40.620
What's this?

00:29:40.980 --> 00:29:43.690
Shinnohara's humanoid computer, of course.

00:29:44.110 --> 00:29:48.950
His data is clean and clear until he reaches his academic and graduate grades.

00:29:48.950 --> 00:29:49.110
It's been erased from his memory.

00:29:50.350 --> 00:29:51.360
It's disgusting.

00:29:52.240 --> 00:29:53.940
Then it's too early to talk about it.

00:29:54.580 --> 00:29:55.480
Why don't we interrogate him first?

00:29:56.790 --> 00:29:57.990
I can't do that.

00:29:58.290 --> 00:29:59.510
You can't? Why?

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:07.640
He was sent to the Shinohara line of Hakobune, but just five days ago, he jumped into the sea.

00:30:08.000 --> 00:30:09.920
His dead body didn't come up.

00:30:10.360 --> 00:30:18.050
It's too late.

00:30:18.370 --> 00:30:19.580
It's just that he's starting to smell bad.

00:30:21.400 --> 00:30:24.020
I wish I could have hit him a little earlier.

00:30:25.160 --> 00:30:29.480
Well, it's a bug. It's a planned crime.

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:32.040
That's why Hoss's suspicions are so deep.

00:30:32.660 --> 00:30:33.800
And the other thing is,

00:30:34.560 --> 00:30:36.800
the developer and the most powerful suspect,

00:30:37.100 --> 00:30:40.630
Mr. Matsui will be the one to clean up the mess.

00:30:40.910 --> 00:30:41.620
Shinohara.

00:30:41.820 --> 00:30:43.200
What's with that face?

00:30:43.500 --> 00:30:45.940
After all, the captain said Hoss was black, right?

00:30:46.720 --> 00:30:48.180
Tetsuyama.

00:30:48.500 --> 00:30:50.200
Don't I look like an idiot?

00:30:51.080 --> 00:30:52.420
Once this is over,

00:30:52.560 --> 00:30:55.910
I want you to continue to analyze the data

00:30:55.910 --> 00:30:56.630
to see what will be the trigger for the rampage.

00:30:56.630 --> 00:30:57.460
Are you up for it?

00:30:57.680 --> 00:30:58.240
I am!

00:30:58.580 --> 00:30:59.350
And then...

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:02.600
Other than the people here, there's no one else in charge of this case.

00:31:02.600 --> 00:31:03.470
Got it?

00:31:04.170 --> 00:31:05.740
Um, why are you asking that?

00:31:05.800 --> 00:31:08.430
Did you forget?

00:31:08.750 --> 00:31:12.360
Last month, Mr. Shige had just rewritten the 98 OS.

00:31:14.830 --> 00:31:18.800
As long as we don't prove that there's nothing going on between him and the boss,

00:31:18.800 --> 00:31:20.760
the 98 is still in danger.

00:31:21.120 --> 00:31:23.380
But if we take action, we won't be able to get out.

00:31:23.480 --> 00:31:26.500
Even if we do that now, we'll just have to give the members no choice.

00:31:27.240 --> 00:31:28.980
Let's go to Hachioji.

00:31:30.380 --> 00:31:33.020
Hey, I just want to make sure.

00:31:33.880 --> 00:31:35.390
I won't get in your way.

00:31:37.100 --> 00:31:38.080
Captain, I'll go too.

00:31:38.380 --> 00:31:39.120
Please let me go.

00:31:39.420 --> 00:31:40.660
You don't have to tell me.

00:31:41.560 --> 00:31:42.140
I'll be in charge!

00:31:42.600 --> 00:31:55.660
What are you doing? Let's go!

00:31:56.540 --> 00:31:56.900
Yes, sir!

00:32:01.820 --> 00:32:02.020
Good.

00:32:02.280 --> 00:32:03.420
We'll go back at night.

00:32:03.540 --> 00:32:05.840
When the expedition is done, I'll command the captain himself.

00:32:07.120 --> 00:32:07.760
No, not that.

00:32:08.200 --> 00:32:10.080
He'll be in trouble if he's involved in the Shinhara.

00:32:11.700 --> 00:32:14.190
He might even be involved with his subordinates.

00:32:14.230 --> 00:32:14.980
I don't know.

00:32:15.000 --> 00:32:15.420
That's a bit ironic.

00:32:15.780 --> 00:32:18.190
My father is the president of the top company in labor,

00:32:18.190 --> 00:32:20.650
and one of his sons is a labor officer.

00:32:20.950 --> 00:32:22.420
And they're both in the military.

00:32:23.240 --> 00:32:26.630
Either way, Shinohara decides.

00:32:27.310 --> 00:32:29.210
I don't like force and orders.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:30.620
That's why.

00:32:36.396 --> 00:32:37.636
Rollout complete.

00:32:37.636 --> 00:32:40.436
Rollout complete on the third and fourth lanes.

00:32:40.780 --> 00:32:41.280
Let's go!

00:32:43.084 --> 00:32:45.084
Thank you for watching!

00:32:45.612 --> 00:32:51.612
The production for the Babylon Project has dropped one step and now the export is the main force.

00:32:51.612 --> 00:32:55.612
The line here has also just increased the operating rate by 20%.

00:32:55.612 --> 00:32:57.612
It's a great feeling.

00:32:58.668 --> 00:32:59.988
This is what I do every day.

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:01.940
It's like a dream to me.

00:33:02.340 --> 00:33:08.970
Shinohara's Eiji and I have been working for the Shinchu army for 50 years.

00:33:09.540 --> 00:33:11.280
We've been manufacturing vehicles and machines.

00:33:11.420 --> 00:33:14.040
When Asuma-san was born, we were working on industrial robots.

00:33:15.500 --> 00:33:16.640
Now, we're working on robots like the labors.

00:33:18.560 --> 00:33:20.540
But I'm not that good at it.

00:33:21.780 --> 00:33:24.190
I've been studying for a long time, but...

00:33:24.510 --> 00:33:25.530
I've been studying for a long time, but...

00:33:25.530 --> 00:33:25.630
I've been studying for a long time, but...

00:33:25.630 --> 00:33:27.230
I've been studying for a long time, but...

00:33:30.480 --> 00:33:31.660
As a technician, I'm lonely.

00:33:32.720 --> 00:33:35.480
What? That's the same thing for me.

00:33:35.720 --> 00:33:37.050
I'm called the god of vehicle maintenance.

00:33:39.390 --> 00:33:42.030
As for the software, it's the same for amateurs.

00:33:42.030 --> 00:33:44.560
I can't do it for people like me.

00:33:45.460 --> 00:33:47.500
Really? What about you, Sakaki-san?

00:33:47.880 --> 00:33:51.600
Even if a technician from a long time ago comforts me, it won't start.

00:33:51.720 --> 00:33:52.790
It's true.

00:33:53.370 --> 00:33:58.080
But no matter how advanced the technology is, it won't change.

00:33:58.380 --> 00:33:59.690
Those who make machines...

00:34:00.650 --> 00:34:04.490
It's not good for the machine if the human side doesn't make a mistake.

00:34:06.690 --> 00:34:12.580
Tsuchiyama-san, today, the manager of the second department came to meet the factory manager of the manufacturer.

00:34:13.400 --> 00:34:16.900
He's been working with the machine for a longer time than his wife.

00:34:17.940 --> 00:34:18.910
I heard it when I was hungry.

00:34:20.770 --> 00:34:23.960
Is the host of the house okay?

00:34:27.400 --> 00:34:29.840
What are you talking about? The host is...

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:32.940
It's a trump card that I sent out with the shogunate.

00:34:33.164 --> 00:34:36.604
It's all over the place, and with Hosu's appearance,

00:34:36.704 --> 00:34:40.264
the success of the Babylon Project has been reduced by 30%.

00:34:40.364 --> 00:34:41.964
Don't ask me that.

00:34:47.244 --> 00:34:48.444
You'll be fine.

00:34:48.716 --> 00:34:50.156
I guarantee it.

00:35:00.190 --> 00:35:01.950
All right, I'm done copying.

00:35:02.230 --> 00:35:10.850
That's a master copy.

00:35:38.060 --> 00:35:38.680
A1

00:35:38.680 --> 00:35:39.870
POPATO

00:35:39.870 --> 00:35:41.840
EHOH

00:36:30.190 --> 00:36:30.930
This is where you're supposed to be.

00:36:31.830 --> 00:36:33.490
No, but if you do that...

00:36:33.490 --> 00:36:33.930
That's enough!

00:36:34.250 --> 00:36:36.710
I'm going to turn off the main computer right now.

00:36:37.150 --> 00:36:38.650
Did you forget that I'm connected to all the other factories?

00:36:40.490 --> 00:36:50.380
I was surprised.

00:36:51.000 --> 00:36:53.630
You didn't leave anything behind, did you?

00:36:53.810 --> 00:36:54.870
Of course not.

00:36:55.070 --> 00:36:58.240
But the only people who know the lock number in that room are me and my grandpa.

00:37:00.120 --> 00:37:02.910
I don't know what's going on there.

00:37:03.270 --> 00:37:04.070
But we've got something.

00:37:05.170 --> 00:37:07.030
It looks like MasterCopy has such a dangerous program.

00:37:08.150 --> 00:37:10.870
Even within Shinohara, Hosu's Protect hasn't been broken.

00:37:12.300 --> 00:37:14.040
The 8,000th generation of Ray-Ban, which is so popular in the prefecture,

00:37:14.040 --> 00:37:15.330
doesn't know what's in it.

00:37:15.810 --> 00:37:18.040
It's a suspicious OS, and it's still in operation.

00:37:18.680 --> 00:37:20.960
It's a bad story, but Asuma,

00:37:21.100 --> 00:37:23.800
good people will start making noise soon.

00:37:24.450 --> 00:37:26.950
Sooner or later, the young lady will notice it too.

00:37:26.990 --> 00:37:28.920
We have to solve it quickly.

00:37:30.190 --> 00:37:30.350
Yes.

00:40:10.270 --> 00:40:10.510
I can see it.

00:40:11.710 --> 00:40:14.830
I can see it from any room.

00:40:15.530 --> 00:40:18.300
But it's not unusual in Tokyo now.

00:40:18.920 --> 00:40:19.790
Isn't it a coincidence?

00:40:20.250 --> 00:40:24.400
More than that, I don't know what kind of man you are.

00:40:25.170 --> 00:40:27.640
You're a high-class labor programmer, aren't you?

00:40:28.590 --> 00:40:29.090
What?

00:40:31.760 --> 00:40:34.080
It's been 26 years since I've been living in such a shabby apartment.

00:40:34.080 --> 00:40:38.150
I don't think it's a good idea to live in this town without leaving any traces.

00:40:38.710 --> 00:40:42.980
It was rebuilt and destroyed, but even if the building remains like this,

00:40:42.980 --> 00:40:45.020
the background is the same, and there is no one to listen to.

00:40:46.140 --> 00:40:47.870
But don't you think it's strange?

00:40:48.760 --> 00:40:50.200
If you were calculating so thoroughly,

00:40:51.280 --> 00:40:54.620
why did you leave the data of the transfer only on the computer of the agency?

00:40:55.400 --> 00:40:57.360
The job is stupid.

00:40:57.360 --> 00:40:59.360
Why don't you sneak into the memory yard at the end of the school year?

00:41:00.280 --> 00:41:00.820
The man who deleted the personal data.

00:41:02.040 --> 00:41:03.190
I'll let you see this.

00:41:03.630 --> 00:41:09.310
Um, Mr. Keiji, are you done?

00:41:09.950 --> 00:41:11.390
Oh, thank you. I'm sorry.

00:41:11.730 --> 00:41:12.010
Huh?

00:41:27.300 --> 00:41:28.930
I don't know if I wanted to show you.

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:30.740
We're the ones who get caught up in the investigation.

00:41:32.140 --> 00:41:34.480
What are you going to show us?

00:41:35.250 --> 00:41:36.410
What are you doing?

00:41:36.790 --> 00:41:40.230
To find out, we have no choice but to go along with it a little longer.

00:41:40.810 --> 00:41:47.750
Matsui-san, is it okay for us to do this?

00:41:48.370 --> 00:41:50.710
If you're the chief, you won't say anything for the rest of your life.

00:41:50.870 --> 00:41:52.600
That's how it's going to be.

00:41:53.060 --> 00:41:54.140
That's what I don't understand.

00:41:54.580 --> 00:41:57.770
How can a person from the investigation department move on a request from the security department?

00:41:58.110 --> 00:41:59.700
That Mr. Gototto...

00:42:00.280 --> 00:42:01.040
Who's that?

00:42:01.160 --> 00:42:02.570
Kamisori Goto.

00:42:02.850 --> 00:42:04.510
He's famous in this town.

00:42:04.890 --> 00:42:05.710
Why is he so sharp?

00:42:06.050 --> 00:42:08.000
Why is he so sharp?

00:42:08.180 --> 00:42:11.140
Because he's too sharp.

00:42:13.930 --> 00:42:14.670
Okay, let's go.

00:42:15.980 --> 00:42:16.380
Hey!

00:42:17.930 --> 00:42:26.280
This is the scene of the crash in the last two months.

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:30.180
You're right.

00:42:31.200 --> 00:42:36.720
Riverside Reconstruction District, Shintoshin, Shinjuku, and Ariake Harbor City.

00:42:38.140 --> 00:42:40.570
But Shinohara, this area used to be full of labor.

00:42:42.130 --> 00:42:46.220
I thought so too, but it's the distribution of labor in the city.

00:42:46.220 --> 00:42:49.680
That's interesting.

00:42:51.230 --> 00:42:52.310
There are other places where labor is concentrated,

00:42:54.610 --> 00:42:58.020
but this very limited area is the only place where accidents occur.

00:42:58.120 --> 00:42:59.980
In other words, in that place...

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:00.780
It means there's something that's causing a rampage.

00:43:02.690 --> 00:43:03.770
So what's going on?

00:43:03.970 --> 00:43:07.620
I'm taking out as much data as I can and dividing the commonality.

00:43:08.880 --> 00:43:10.220
The conditions are too vague.

00:43:12.200 --> 00:43:15.260
If Shige-san were to tell me at a time like this...

00:43:15.260 --> 00:43:19.290
Shinohara, why don't you take a little break?

00:43:19.670 --> 00:43:21.560
You're not sleeping at night, are you?

00:43:21.830 --> 00:43:22.590
I can't do that.

00:43:22.990 --> 00:43:25.290
I don't know when the 98 earthquake will happen.

00:43:26.190 --> 00:43:27.120
It's okay.

00:43:27.300 --> 00:43:28.400
Take a breath of the air outside.

00:43:30.960 --> 00:43:35.830
The hope of yesterday, the hope of today, and the reality of tomorrow are taking one step at a time.

00:43:37.630 --> 00:43:42.910
For a prosperous tomorrow, Babylon Project is a challenge for the 21st century.

00:44:00.060 --> 00:44:03.540
What are you talking about? You look like you don't have enough vitamins.

00:44:04.620 --> 00:44:06.690
I need to get some more guts.

00:44:07.850 --> 00:44:14.650
Did you wash it properly?

00:44:14.990 --> 00:44:23.430
Noah, go out with her.

00:44:23.570 --> 00:44:25.020
What are you talking about?

00:44:25.080 --> 00:44:26.590
Come on! Let's go on a date!

00:44:27.370 --> 00:44:27.870
Hey!

00:44:28.460 --> 00:44:28.860
Hey!

00:44:31.560 --> 00:44:40.980
You gave me permission, didn't you?

00:44:41.360 --> 00:44:44.700
The captain told me to breathe in the air outside.

00:44:44.880 --> 00:44:46.360
You gave me permission, didn't you?

00:44:46.560 --> 00:44:48.590
But you two are still in uniform.

00:44:49.490 --> 00:44:52.060
And you're in a no-hell, two-seater.

00:44:52.500 --> 00:44:54.580
This is really bad, isn't it?

00:44:54.760 --> 00:44:55.480
I don't care.

00:44:55.880 --> 00:44:58.340
I've checked the patrol time of the patrol car properly.

00:45:00.190 --> 00:45:01.630
That's not what I'm talking about!

00:45:01.730 --> 00:45:02.070
What?

00:45:02.370 --> 00:45:04.320
That's not what I'm talking about!

00:45:05.160 --> 00:45:06.840
Then what are you talking about?

00:45:07.120 --> 00:45:08.820
Forget it! I'm going to beat you up!

00:45:08.980 --> 00:45:09.800
Leave it to me!

00:45:10.080 --> 00:45:15.860
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:45:15.920 --> 00:45:18.780
This is a 20-inch special five-leaf pizza.

00:45:18.880 --> 00:45:19.780
It's an ethnic style.

00:45:20.790 --> 00:45:21.250
Amazing.

00:45:23.460 --> 00:45:24.840
Hey, are you really okay?

00:45:25.220 --> 00:45:26.720
You look like you're standing out.

00:45:27.240 --> 00:45:28.200
Don't be scared.

00:45:28.900 --> 00:45:29.740
Don't make that face.

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:30.820
There's no problem with that.

00:45:30.820 --> 00:45:31.520
That's right.

00:45:31.760 --> 00:45:33.600
Well then, let's eat.

00:45:36.480 --> 00:45:38.620
But, why did you suddenly want to treat me?

00:45:40.480 --> 00:45:41.850
Well, just a little.

00:45:44.420 --> 00:45:44.840
Hey, Noah.

00:45:45.060 --> 00:45:45.280
What?

00:45:46.090 --> 00:45:49.180
How's Alphonse doing lately?

00:45:49.930 --> 00:45:53.400
Of course, he's doing great.

00:45:53.820 --> 00:45:55.620
Why do you ask such a question?

00:45:56.290 --> 00:45:58.460
Well, I was wondering how he was doing.

00:45:58.620 --> 00:45:59.840
Alphonse is...

00:46:00.060 --> 00:46:01.000
It's always the best.

00:46:01.460 --> 00:46:05.190
Mr. Sakaki and the maintenance team will do their best to maintain it.

00:46:05.670 --> 00:46:10.620
Listen to me and move properly.

00:46:10.800 --> 00:46:12.520
I'm not going to run away.

00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:30.480
I knew you were listening.

00:46:30.860 --> 00:46:34.840
Hey, it's okay.

00:46:35.440 --> 00:46:37.200
Albonce doesn't run wild, does he?

00:46:37.760 --> 00:46:38.990
I don't know.

00:46:39.070 --> 00:46:41.160
What makes him run wild?

00:46:41.580 --> 00:46:44.060
The only man who knew that was dead.

00:46:44.640 --> 00:46:46.940
We haven't found the answer yet.

00:46:47.840 --> 00:46:49.860
Then let's rewrite the OS.

00:46:50.220 --> 00:46:51.720
If we don't have that host...

00:46:51.720 --> 00:46:54.410
To rewrite the OS, we'll have to ask the manufacturer.

00:46:55.370 --> 00:46:57.450
For that, we need official documents.

00:46:57.970 --> 00:46:59.650
The mechanism of the run...

00:47:00.000 --> 00:47:02.670
As long as we don't prove it, the higher-ups won't allow us to do it.

00:47:03.230 --> 00:47:05.050
But we can't just let it go like this.

00:47:05.290 --> 00:47:10.300
If Alphonse runs away, then Alphonse will be torn apart, right?

00:47:10.580 --> 00:47:12.440
Just like the labor that Ota-san and I destroyed.

00:47:14.900 --> 00:47:18.000
Hey, Noah, give me a little more time.

00:47:18.200 --> 00:47:20.030
I'll find the answer for sure.

00:47:24.860 --> 00:47:27.360
Forward and backup are one and the same.

00:47:27.560 --> 00:47:29.970
The pilot is Shiki-

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:30.900
You must obey the order of the king.

00:47:31.610 --> 00:47:32.690
Asma, you're so stubborn.

00:47:34.090 --> 00:47:35.490
Come on, let's eat.

00:47:35.770 --> 00:47:36.580
You'll wake up.

00:47:36.920 --> 00:47:46.560
Alphonse is just like him.

00:47:46.840 --> 00:47:47.060
What?

00:47:47.240 --> 00:47:48.780
Alphonse I.

00:47:49.080 --> 00:47:50.580
The dog I had when I was little.

00:47:51.860 --> 00:47:52.360
What?

00:47:52.780 --> 00:47:54.080
So that's II?

00:47:54.340 --> 00:47:55.880
Too bad.

00:47:55.920 --> 00:47:56.320
III.

00:47:56.620 --> 00:47:57.920
II was a cat.

00:48:00.220 --> 00:48:01.220
Hm? What is it?

00:48:02.350 --> 00:48:03.490
I can hear something.

00:48:03.850 --> 00:48:06.660
The dog's ears can also hear sounds that humans can't hear.

00:48:08.020 --> 00:48:10.180
I think the wind is blowing somewhere.

00:48:10.740 --> 00:48:13.590
The wind is blowing?

00:48:15.060 --> 00:48:17.040
What's wrong? You suddenly look weird.

00:48:17.860 --> 00:48:25.440
The wind and sounds that humans can't hear.

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:32.670
I'm going to borrow this. I need to check something.

00:48:33.130 --> 00:48:36.370
Borrow? Then how do I get home?

00:48:36.810 --> 00:48:39.760
And when you get home, tell the captain to wait for my call.

00:48:41.100 --> 00:48:42.020
See you!

00:48:42.320 --> 00:48:59.980
My father couldn't be caught, so...

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:02.700
The head office doesn't tell me anything.

00:49:02.940 --> 00:49:06.770
When I call my family, they say they haven't been back in a while.

00:49:07.230 --> 00:49:08.480
They're always busy.

00:49:09.460 --> 00:49:11.210
I'm sorry to bother you.

00:49:11.610 --> 00:49:13.460
My daughter is back with her child.

00:49:14.460 --> 00:49:15.630
Your grandfather's grandchild?

00:49:15.930 --> 00:49:17.850
You can't just drink beer when you're on duty.

00:49:17.990 --> 00:49:19.330
You can drink coffee right now.

00:49:20.220 --> 00:49:22.640
How many hertz of sound does it make the labor run out?

00:49:24.440 --> 00:49:25.980
Tell me that.

00:49:32.940 --> 00:49:34.520
The Sumitomo Building in Shinto-shin, Shinjuku.

00:49:34.820 --> 00:49:36.760
The Twin Building in Riverside Park Town 21.

00:49:38.470 --> 00:49:41.690
When the wind blows, both of them blow low-frequency like a big whistle.

00:49:42.130 --> 00:49:44.690
It's a high-frequency building with a blowing-out structure.

00:49:44.770 --> 00:49:47.920
And there's a harpy bridge that connects Daiba and Shiba-Ura.

00:49:49.140 --> 00:49:51.750
The wire crossing the bridge should be blowing in the wind.

00:49:52.510 --> 00:49:54.390
It's a sound that humans can't hear.

00:49:54.670 --> 00:49:57.170
It's a sound that only labor's sensitive sensors can hear.

00:49:57.410 --> 00:49:59.960
That's what this series of rampant accidents is all about.

00:50:00.680 --> 00:50:07.260
The labor work environment is easy to produce this kind of sound, and it is concentrated in the city and large construction sites.

00:50:08.000 --> 00:50:12.670
The man who chose low frequency for the trigger of the rampage is certainly smart.

00:50:13.860 --> 00:50:16.920
It shouldn't be a coincidence that he got a job at Shinohara Jukou in this industry.

00:50:18.810 --> 00:50:22.030
The old man, who opposed the major manufacturer and was impatient with the sound of the market,

00:50:24.180 --> 00:50:25.160
presumably jumped on the food.

00:50:26.200 --> 00:50:29.490
And now he realized his identity and was in a hurry.

00:50:30.890 --> 00:50:34.050
As I thought, Rayburn's O.S. has become one of the hosses.

00:50:34.390 --> 00:50:36.390
On the contrary, it's trying to be a bird of death.

00:50:37.230 --> 00:50:39.950
It's because my father can't be caught.

00:50:40.030 --> 00:50:41.090
That's why I'm on the run.

00:50:41.490 --> 00:50:45.290
Asuma-san, if that's announced now, Shinohara will...

00:50:45.290 --> 00:50:49.950
Uncle, even if it's not me,

00:50:51.120 --> 00:50:52.620
Someone will come to the same conclusion sooner or later.

00:50:53.650 --> 00:50:55.420
I want you to announce this from your uncle's mouth.

00:50:57.120 --> 00:50:59.600
Rayburn is a villain.

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:00.820
You can't do that, right?

00:51:31.720 --> 00:51:32.040
Bastard!

00:51:32.730 --> 00:51:33.450
It was a close call!

00:51:33.710 --> 00:51:35.750
Your precious sacrifice was not in vain!

00:51:47.920 --> 00:51:50.080
Ordering the inspector Shinohara to stay at home for two weeks.

00:51:50.560 --> 00:51:52.830
You know the reason, don't you?

00:51:53.650 --> 00:51:54.910
I don't know!

00:51:55.250 --> 00:51:56.290
Then I'll tell you.

00:51:56.390 --> 00:51:59.780
He went to the general public house without permission.

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:01.920
He is a self-proclaimed tyrant.

00:52:01.940 --> 00:52:03.640
He uses his wife's computer without permission.

00:52:03.940 --> 00:52:04.960
He is a friend of his colleague.

00:52:05.160 --> 00:52:06.360
He drives a two-seater car.

00:52:06.360 --> 00:52:07.000
He is a drunkard.

00:52:07.020 --> 00:52:07.480
He is a driver.

00:52:08.880 --> 00:52:09.880
There are many more violations.

00:52:09.940 --> 00:52:12.360
He should be punished for his insolent behavior.

00:52:14.200 --> 00:52:15.380
It's time for him to be punished.

00:52:15.560 --> 00:52:16.840
He put in Captain Goto's words.

00:52:17.320 --> 00:52:17.580
And he was punished.

00:52:18.660 --> 00:52:19.940
Even though he is an incompetent subordinate,

00:52:20.260 --> 00:52:21.920
he should be grateful for his kindness.

00:52:22.880 --> 00:52:23.840
That's all.

00:52:24.100 --> 00:52:25.160
I have a question.

00:52:25.660 --> 00:52:26.820
What about Shinohara Jukou?

00:52:27.320 --> 00:52:28.720
That has nothing to do with you.

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:32.700
At this rate, you'll wake up, too.

00:52:33.380 --> 00:52:35.900
It's not something you should be worried about.

00:52:36.480 --> 00:52:39.210
Last night, the president of Shinohara Jukou

00:52:39.210 --> 00:52:42.790
reported that there was a serious problem with the HOS.

00:52:44.550 --> 00:52:46.610
The government focused on the situation.

00:52:46.650 --> 00:52:51.150
This morning, Shinohara's request was received.

00:52:51.290 --> 00:52:53.770
The decision was made to switch to the old OS as soon as possible.

00:52:56.230 --> 00:52:58.220
In addition, it should be prevented from unnecessary confusion.

00:53:00.400 --> 00:53:03.510
This will be announced as a free copy of the new version of HOS.

00:53:04.950 --> 00:53:05.490
That's stupid!

00:53:06.360 --> 00:53:07.020
What will happen to the responsibility of Shirohara Junko?

00:53:08.000 --> 00:53:09.800
I was the only one who was disposed of, and the other side is a man.

00:53:10.460 --> 00:53:10.840
Is it okay to fight?

00:53:12.580 --> 00:53:14.280
What the hell are you thinking of the police?

00:53:15.720 --> 00:53:17.800
Investigation is not the means of parent-child quarrels.

00:53:18.440 --> 00:53:20.320
A criminal who doesn't even have the right to investigate.

00:53:20.780 --> 00:53:23.160
If you don't get permission from your boss, you can't do your own investigation.

00:53:23.860 --> 00:53:25.080
What's wrong with you?

00:53:34.280 --> 00:53:38.540
I think it would be better for the government to admit the fire and send it out, rather than being dragged out by the outside world and pursued.

00:53:38.540 --> 00:53:45.140
For the government, it is a problem that the eyes of the world turn to the labor system itself rather than Shinohara.

00:53:45.420 --> 00:53:47.470
Because the Babylon Project is involved.

00:53:47.930 --> 00:53:50.980
On the day the fire is lit, the fire will burn in our hearts.

00:53:51.680 --> 00:53:54.860
If that's the case, I'd rather put Shinohara in the dark and erase everything.

00:53:56.240 --> 00:53:57.590
Well, that's about it.

00:53:57.830 --> 00:53:59.560
Well, don't be so depressed.

00:54:00.600 --> 00:54:01.440
You did a good job.

00:54:01.720 --> 00:54:03.180
Even though we had all the data,

00:54:03.820 --> 00:54:04.980
you were too self-sufficient to be so dangerous.

00:54:06.140 --> 00:54:07.490
You were too naive.

00:54:08.050 --> 00:54:09.800
But I wonder why the chief

00:54:09.800 --> 00:54:11.700
knew about the two of you.

00:54:12.860 --> 00:54:13.880
Oh, that.

00:54:14.080 --> 00:54:15.550
Dr. Izumi told me.

00:54:16.390 --> 00:54:16.830
Captain!

00:54:18.550 --> 00:54:20.790
You're tired, aren't you?

00:54:20.830 --> 00:54:22.760
Now you can leave the scene and concentrate on the investigation.

00:54:24.700 --> 00:54:26.610
Are you still going to investigate?

00:54:26.830 --> 00:54:28.580
You're young, but you're so naive.

00:54:30.540 --> 00:54:33.840
Shinohara, the head of the party, has not yet been able to understand the whole situation, including Hosu.

00:54:34.800 --> 00:54:36.900
If the exchange would end in a simple way,

00:54:38.000 --> 00:54:40.160
There was no need for Hoba to take his own life.

00:54:40.900 --> 00:54:41.960
Isn't that right?

00:54:42.160 --> 00:54:45.260
The captain still believes in Hoba's position.

00:54:46.940 --> 00:54:49.220
How about you, Shinohara?

00:54:49.980 --> 00:54:51.850
I think so, too.

00:54:52.520 --> 00:54:53.140
Asuma!

00:54:53.300 --> 00:54:56.110
I'm back!

00:54:56.790 --> 00:54:58.680
Mr. Shige!

00:55:02.840 --> 00:55:03.800
What's wrong with that dress?

00:55:03.960 --> 00:55:05.620
What's wrong with Asuma's dress?

00:55:06.620 --> 00:55:08.230
No, there's a lot of that.

00:55:08.390 --> 00:55:09.750
I got two weeks of prohibition.

00:55:10.490 --> 00:55:12.540
It's because I'm thinking about teamwork and I'm alone.

00:55:13.940 --> 00:55:15.200
If you'd consulted us for a minute,

00:55:15.820 --> 00:55:16.840
It wouldn't have happened.

00:55:17.600 --> 00:55:19.000
Where did you get your teamwork?

00:55:19.400 --> 00:55:19.820
I'm getting a line.

00:55:21.080 --> 00:55:21.440
What?

00:55:22.240 --> 00:55:23.800
Well, well, well, well, well, well, well, well, well, well, well, well, well, well, well, well, well, well, well, well, well.

00:55:23.980 --> 00:55:25.600
This is a happy return.

00:55:25.820 --> 00:55:26.940
I'm going to stand up.

00:55:27.200 --> 00:55:28.100
You're welcome.

00:55:28.720 --> 00:55:29.700
That's more than you.

00:55:30.090 --> 00:55:32.190
Hurry up and apply for a replacement, please.

00:55:32.670 --> 00:55:33.430
Oh, that's right.

00:55:33.510 --> 00:55:35.610
I'm sorry I'm back so soon, but I'm counting on you.

00:55:35.900 --> 00:55:36.540
Replacement?

00:55:36.720 --> 00:55:37.040
Yes.

00:55:37.240 --> 00:55:38.220
Of the 98 model.

00:55:38.540 --> 00:55:38.940
Of the OS!

00:55:39.240 --> 00:55:39.580
Huh?

00:55:41.880 --> 00:55:42.700
What are you thinking?

00:55:43.280 --> 00:55:44.330
It's not good to keep the hose piled up.

00:55:45.230 --> 00:55:47.120
That's why I tried my best to remember to die.

00:55:47.440 --> 00:55:48.230
I even got an injection.

00:55:48.970 --> 00:55:50.930
I'm not doing a replacement for the hose.

00:55:51.530 --> 00:55:52.380
No way!

00:55:52.440 --> 00:55:53.790
Because of the director's instructions.

00:55:54.360 --> 00:55:55.740
That's why I pretended to rewrite it.

00:55:56.100 --> 00:55:56.940
I threw it into the dummy of the mobile screen.

00:55:58.040 --> 00:55:59.280
I sent the diskette back as it was.

00:56:01.052 --> 00:56:05.092
The inside is the same as before, but it's not good at all, right?

00:56:05.148 --> 00:56:05.648
Hmm?

00:56:06.204 --> 00:56:06.704
Yeah!

00:56:06.780 --> 00:56:08.780
When they find out that the hoss is in trouble,

00:56:08.780 --> 00:56:09.280
YAKA!

00:56:09.436 --> 00:56:12.436
This is also an educational tool for parents.

00:56:12.436 --> 00:56:17.436
No matter how useful it is, I can't get used to it.

00:56:17.728 --> 00:56:20.348
Every day, I'm the only one who's guilty.

00:56:20.412 --> 00:56:23.332
Tie that secret to your nose and fly!

00:56:23.356 --> 00:56:26.276
Well, I think it's the right thing to do.

00:56:26.908 --> 00:56:28.268
Really? No one is listening?

00:56:29.500 --> 00:56:30.000
That's weird.

00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:33.920
I talked about it when Goto-san got an international phone call.

00:56:34.260 --> 00:56:35.300
To the captain?

00:56:35.680 --> 00:56:37.120
That's that.

00:56:37.640 --> 00:56:41.520
If you keep quiet about it, Asuma-san will be willing to die and work hard.

00:56:41.740 --> 00:56:43.660
It's a pattern that he's thinking about.

00:56:44.900 --> 00:56:47.000
What do I think of Noah?

00:56:47.000 --> 00:56:49.060
He played with the light and shadow of youth.

00:56:49.980 --> 00:56:50.980
That bastard.

00:56:51.540 --> 00:56:53.100
Poor Asuma.

00:56:54.100 --> 00:56:55.600
I'll teach you a lesson!

00:58:10.750 --> 00:58:20.380
It's in English, isn't it?

00:58:21.410 --> 00:58:23.020
He descends from heaven.

00:58:23.820 --> 00:58:24.780
Ehova.

00:58:24.920 --> 00:58:26.080
He descends from heaven.

00:58:28.090 --> 00:58:29.970
Kura Kikoto Hanahada.

00:58:30.000 --> 00:58:31.790
It's one of the four volumes of the Old Testament.

00:58:33.150 --> 00:58:36.110
I'm sure it's something that the owner wrote.

00:58:38.090 --> 00:58:40.590
Anyway, you've been looking for it since you were born.

00:58:42.190 --> 00:58:43.820
What? After moving out?

00:58:45.120 --> 00:58:45.460
I just got there.

00:58:46.500 --> 00:58:48.020
But this is the end.

00:58:48.080 --> 00:58:49.100
That's the dead end.

00:58:49.420 --> 00:58:53.940
That's the part of the city that was destroyed by the earthquake in the 1980s.

00:58:57.290 --> 00:58:59.440
The holy place of the national road law.

00:59:00.090 --> 00:59:04.550
In the end, it was a land that was floating in the middle without being used.

00:59:07.600 --> 00:59:09.080
It's a strange town.

00:59:09.440 --> 00:59:14.870
While chasing after his past, I felt like I was left behind in the flow of time.

00:59:17.020 --> 00:59:21.680
The scenery that I had been used to until now has been destroyed over and over again.

00:59:23.040 --> 00:59:24.850
When I look away for a moment, it's all gone.

00:59:26.230 --> 00:59:28.310
And it's faster than I thought.

00:59:30.830 --> 00:59:34.000
Maybe the past has nothing to do with this place.

00:59:34.480 --> 00:59:38.940
The place we're talking about was a sea a little while ago.

00:59:39.820 --> 00:59:44.400
In a few years, a huge city will be born in this sea in front of us.

00:59:44.420 --> 00:59:48.620
But that's going to be the past without a single thing to do with it.

00:59:49.340 --> 00:59:51.310
It's like you're dating a bad joke.

00:59:52.570 --> 00:59:55.010
Maybe that's what you wanted to show me.

01:00:01.720 --> 01:00:04.320
Where are we going? Who are we?

01:00:05.060 --> 01:00:06.080
What's that?

01:00:06.480 --> 01:00:13.210
A long time ago, a bandit commander who attacked Europe and destroyed it wrote a complaint on the wall.

01:00:16.300 --> 01:00:16.900
Bad boy!

01:00:16.900 --> 01:00:18.440
Doji, go to the pit!

01:00:18.820 --> 01:00:19.840
See you.

01:00:20.220 --> 01:00:22.060
Sorry, I said too much.

01:00:31.020 --> 01:00:33.120
Finally, can you tell me about Mr. Matsui's new book?

01:00:34.560 --> 01:00:36.500
It's black, Mr. Goto.

01:00:36.780 --> 01:00:37.920
It's definitely black.

01:00:39.130 --> 01:00:41.650
But if Hoshi is dead one step ahead,

01:00:41.830 --> 01:00:43.320
That's as far as we're going.

01:00:44.360 --> 01:00:47.050
Well, I'll take this loan one day.

01:00:47.070 --> 01:00:47.960
Mentally

01:00:47.960 --> 01:00:49.990
It's a good thing.

01:00:50.490 --> 01:00:52.320
Tomato field, chicken coop,

01:00:52.400 --> 01:00:53.940
The security guard is fishing with his bare hands.

01:00:54.560 --> 01:00:58.140
Is this really a police station?

01:00:58.820 --> 01:00:59.660
A police station?

01:01:00.120 --> 01:01:02.750
I'm more of a friend of justice.

01:01:03.370 --> 01:01:07.510
Do you think you're still overthinking?

01:01:08.240 --> 01:01:10.250
I wonder.

01:01:10.790 --> 01:01:13.110
I think there's something wrong with the spirit.

01:01:15.000 --> 01:01:16.120
I'm grateful for that.

01:01:16.920 --> 01:01:18.920
I asked Kanuka in NY about the MIT-era

01:01:18.920 --> 01:01:20.400
I asked him about the old house.

01:01:20.900 --> 01:01:22.430
Apparently, he was called a god.

01:01:23.650 --> 01:01:24.500
A god?

01:01:25.100 --> 01:01:25.840
The name of a god in the Old Testament.

01:01:27.380 --> 01:01:29.800
His name is similar to that of a genius.

01:01:29.800 --> 01:01:29.960
Thank you for watching!

01:01:30.000 --> 01:01:30.740
I don't think it was a big deal.

01:01:31.140 --> 01:01:33.670
However, there is a mistake in this.

01:01:33.850 --> 01:01:37.300
To be precise, it is correct to pronounce Yahweh or Yahweh.

01:01:38.480 --> 01:01:41.760
It seems that Ehoa is a way of reading that has been spread by mistake.

01:01:42.200 --> 01:01:46.140
It seems that Hoban was surprised to hear that.

01:01:46.280 --> 01:01:51.640
I feel like I finally understand Shinobu-san and Hoban's way of thinking.

01:01:54.220 --> 01:01:58.700
What kind of crime do you plan to commit by looking up at the high-rise building from the window of the room on the day you come?

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:06.700
Ehova, go down and see the city and the tower where the people stand.

01:02:06.900 --> 01:02:10.520
Now, we will go down.

01:02:10.600 --> 01:02:14.610
We will read their words and communicate with each other.

01:02:15.690 --> 01:02:21.260
That's why it's called Babel.

01:02:23.100 --> 01:02:26.540
But it's a coincidence.

01:02:27.020 --> 01:02:29.640
I didn't dare choose Hakobune when my aunt was dying.

01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:30.520
Is it a coincidence?

01:02:30.880 --> 01:02:32.960
If everything is based on the Bible's code,

01:02:34.360 --> 01:02:36.340
the target will not be able to steal the Babylon Project.

01:02:37.380 --> 01:02:39.720
What a disaster, Babylon.

01:02:40.960 --> 01:02:43.480
The God's image was destroyed and scattered on the ground.

01:02:43.540 --> 01:02:44.970
If you give it to me, I'll give it to you.

01:02:45.000 --> 01:02:45.460
It's still coming out.

01:02:45.600 --> 01:02:47.570
It's a message he left on purpose.

01:02:48.030 --> 01:02:49.610
For example, there's this one.

01:02:49.930 --> 01:02:56.310
The 26 places on the map are all over the three runaway target areas that Asuma found.

01:02:56.850 --> 01:02:58.570
Matsui-san was also curious.

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:02.140
It's just a trick to solve the mystery.

01:03:02.560 --> 01:03:03.180
A challenge?

01:03:03.600 --> 01:03:04.560
He's not that romantic.

01:03:05.380 --> 01:03:08.190
The police won't take him for granted.

01:03:08.330 --> 01:03:12.080
He had absolute confidence in his program.

01:03:13.240 --> 01:03:15.440
Otherwise, he wouldn't have died without looking at the results.

01:03:16.400 --> 01:03:22.900
He must have jumped off while praising all the people who live in this town.

01:03:24.610 --> 01:03:28.010
Hey, are you aware?

01:03:29.260 --> 01:03:29.960
You're the only one...

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:32.100
He looks very happy when he talks to his aunt.

01:03:32.680 --> 01:03:34.560
That's dangerous.

01:03:34.900 --> 01:03:35.380
Really?

01:03:36.230 --> 01:03:40.260
But if it's such a plan,

01:03:40.540 --> 01:03:41.340
Is it okay to leave it to those two?

01:03:42.640 --> 01:03:44.000
I think it's okay.

01:03:44.380 --> 01:03:55.680
I'm sleepy and tired.

01:03:56.900 --> 01:03:59.270
All right, it's over.

01:04:03.900 --> 01:04:04.280
Let's go.

01:04:04.520 --> 01:04:05.120
It's fast.

01:04:05.360 --> 01:04:11.430
What's the parameter of the simulation program?

01:04:12.510 --> 01:04:14.170
If there's no mistake in the number 10.21Hz,

01:04:15.650 --> 01:04:16.600
this should be right.

01:04:16.980 --> 01:04:19.620
Then, the damage to the forecast is this much.

01:04:19.920 --> 01:04:22.240
If this is the case, we might have to close our eyes and make a deal.

01:04:33.580 --> 01:04:34.720
There's no way it's going to be like this.

01:04:35.540 --> 01:04:37.310
What data is missing?

01:04:38.050 --> 01:04:38.940
The file that was in the hoss.

01:04:41.940 --> 01:04:43.660
If we can get rid of that,

01:04:43.660 --> 01:04:45.210
We can prove that Mr. Godo said it was a crime.

01:04:47.230 --> 01:04:48.750
I'm sure we can get more people and equipment.

01:04:50.310 --> 01:04:52.000
What about Troy's wood?

01:04:52.280 --> 01:04:52.700
Maybe.

01:04:53.440 --> 01:04:56.380
Maybe it was rewritten and the stain spread even more.

01:04:57.530 --> 01:04:58.730
I made a stupid decision.

01:05:02.170 --> 01:05:07.430
Oh, I got it.

01:05:08.370 --> 01:05:09.050
It's just that we're powerless.

01:05:10.030 --> 01:05:10.490
What?

01:05:11.580 --> 01:05:13.180
Here's the newspaper.

01:05:13.480 --> 01:05:14.060
Thank you.

01:05:14.740 --> 01:05:16.740
Now then, what's the status of the world?

01:05:17.280 --> 01:05:20.190
If God is my opponent, I'm like a computer boy.

01:05:21.970 --> 01:05:24.520
Hey, I want coffee.

01:05:24.860 --> 01:05:25.550
That's nice.

01:05:25.990 --> 01:05:27.070
I only have instant coffee.

01:05:27.670 --> 01:05:28.290
Yes, yes.

01:05:30.670 --> 01:05:41.150
Turn it on!

01:05:41.370 --> 01:05:41.590
Huh?

01:05:41.830 --> 01:05:42.960
Hurry up!

01:05:43.330 --> 01:05:44.430
What the hell are you talking about?

01:05:44.790 --> 01:05:49.910
Is something wrong with this?

01:06:00.700 --> 01:06:01.240
What's going on?

01:06:01.480 --> 01:06:01.940
It's resonance, resonance.

01:06:02.300 --> 01:06:06.180
It's meaningless to simulate a low-frequency source with individual data.

01:06:07.400 --> 01:06:10.440
If the resonance phenomenon occurs,

01:06:10.660 --> 01:06:12.820
it will interfere with each other and be amplified.

01:06:13.320 --> 01:06:19.430
It doesn't change.

01:06:20.620 --> 01:06:23.360
The low-frequency source, which is the first trigger, is too weak.

01:06:24.220 --> 01:06:25.640
We have to use a more powerful one.

01:06:26.520 --> 01:06:27.950
A blown-out building.

01:06:28.130 --> 01:06:28.830
A harpy bridge.

01:06:29.110 --> 01:06:29.510
An iron skeleton at a construction site.

01:06:30.320 --> 01:06:31.560
And the underground facility's vent.

01:06:31.860 --> 01:06:33.270
What else could there be?

01:06:33.430 --> 01:06:35.060
Well, if you think about it,

01:06:35.060 --> 01:06:35.520
it's in a place where there's no interference,

01:06:36.880 --> 01:06:38.280
and there's a lot of air.

01:06:38.360 --> 01:06:38.900
That's right.

01:06:39.280 --> 01:06:41.640
If there's a multi-layered structure or something...

01:06:41.640 --> 01:06:43.800
That's what this dense Tokyo...

01:06:43.800 --> 01:06:44.040
Hey!

01:07:00.480 --> 01:07:01.320
This guy is so annoying!

01:07:02.180 --> 01:07:04.060
I forgot to take a copy of it in Hachioji.

01:07:04.220 --> 01:07:06.990
After inserting this data into the wind tunnel simulation program,

01:07:08.110 --> 01:07:10.930
I'll take the wind speed variable value unlimitedly and input it.

01:07:11.430 --> 01:07:12.340
This is...

01:07:12.340 --> 01:07:13.660
It's not going to be easy here.

01:07:14.240 --> 01:07:18.710
All right, it's connected!

01:07:41.230 --> 01:07:44.860
At that time, the speed of the moment was 40 meters.

01:07:45.140 --> 01:07:48.880
If you don't land in a typhoon, you can't fly.

01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:02.520
We are heading to Hokokuto at a speed of 25 km per hour.

01:08:03.700 --> 01:08:06.780
We will land in Tokyo Bay on the day after tomorrow.

01:08:07.000 --> 01:08:09.340
The air pressure is 950 millibars.

01:08:09.540 --> 01:08:11.420
Within 20 km radius from the center,

01:08:11.420 --> 01:08:12.920
the wind speed will reach more than 40 meters.

01:08:14.680 --> 01:08:16.660
That's enough! Stop it!

01:08:16.960 --> 01:08:19.200
All of this is just a rumor.

01:08:19.840 --> 01:08:24.240
If you ask me, this simulator was developed by a labor team

01:08:24.240 --> 01:08:25.540
with the maintenance staff.

01:08:27.400 --> 01:08:28.500
Do you believe that?

01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:31.020
Are you seriously thinking about it?

01:08:31.340 --> 01:08:33.020
According to the weather forecast,

01:08:33.900 --> 01:08:36.780
Typhoon 19 will hit the capital city unannounced on the 5th day of the month.

01:08:38.340 --> 01:08:39.140
There is no time to request a program notification.

01:08:40.320 --> 01:08:41.800
It is said that it is only possible,

01:08:42.360 --> 01:08:45.790
but it is also true that there is no reason to deny it so far.

01:08:50.080 --> 01:08:51.420
Due to the strong wind due to the landing of the typhoon,

01:08:51.420 --> 01:08:52.640
Hakobune is in a daze.

01:08:53.140 --> 01:08:56.700
In addition to that, hundreds of high-altitude ships,

01:08:56.780 --> 01:08:58.240
which are attracted by it, raise the direction of the low-frequency wave,

01:08:58.520 --> 01:08:59.780
and the capital city is in a state of 8,000.

01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:03.320
I don't think it's necessary to tell you what the result will be.

01:09:05.510 --> 01:09:11.920
Not only Wangan and the redevelopment district in the city, but also the geofront work area 1,000 meters underground.

01:09:11.920 --> 01:09:14.080
In addition, labor is in motion in some of the nuclear power plants.

01:09:16.160 --> 01:09:19.730
If this simulator becomes a reality,

01:09:20.500 --> 01:09:24.120
I would like to ask you who will be the scapegoat for the third time or the responsibility that could not prevent the crime in advance.

01:09:30.220 --> 01:09:34.720
Gotoh-kun, the labor OS rewriting process in the capital is already complete.

01:09:35.930 --> 01:09:39.410
Even if there is a Hover A1 crime plan that you're talking about,

01:09:39.490 --> 01:09:42.470
it's actually not working, isn't it?

01:09:42.690 --> 01:09:45.740
The identity of the HOS is still unknown, although it is being analyzed with the help of MIT.

01:09:48.030 --> 01:09:52.210
The possibility of the labor being trapped in the memory of the main body cannot be denied.

01:09:52.470 --> 01:09:54.090
The expert's opinion is the same.

01:09:54.430 --> 01:09:57.480
At this time, the labor that has been in contact with the HOS once

01:09:57.480 --> 01:09:58.540
is considered to be contaminated.

01:10:00.060 --> 01:10:06.680
Will you change the course of the typhoon, knock down the high-altitude layer, or dismantle the 8,000 laborers?

01:10:07.600 --> 01:10:10.130
Or do you agree with all four?

01:10:10.970 --> 01:10:12.540
Please make a decision.

01:10:12.940 --> 01:10:17.440
The period from today until the typhoon passes.

01:10:18.700 --> 01:10:20.980
All laborers in the city must be banned.

01:10:22.060 --> 01:10:25.010
The production and repair lines of laborers must be stopped during the same period.

01:10:26.030 --> 01:10:29.690
The fire department, the defense department, as well as the neighboring countries...

01:10:30.000 --> 01:10:31.980
We'll explain it to them and ask for their help.

01:10:32.540 --> 01:10:32.860
That's all.

01:10:35.030 --> 01:10:39.020
Captain, the radar that's stopped can also be activated automatically

01:10:39.080 --> 01:10:39.820
by the interference of the low frequency.

01:10:40.820 --> 01:10:43.150
Have you forgotten about the satellite radar of the Self-Defense Force?

01:10:44.190 --> 01:10:45.560
Goto-kun!

01:10:45.640 --> 01:10:46.480
What are you talking about?

01:10:47.070 --> 01:10:49.050
I haven't received such a report, but...

01:10:49.580 --> 01:10:50.460
Then I have another question.

01:10:51.300 --> 01:10:51.960
Shut up!

01:10:52.460 --> 01:10:55.200
If the typhoon calmed down,

01:10:56.320 --> 01:10:57.640
I don't think it's a problem of responsibility.

01:11:00.000 --> 01:11:01.960
But it's going to be a typhoon.

01:11:04.200 --> 01:11:06.530
Of course.

01:11:06.750 --> 01:11:07.420
It can't be helped if it's a genius.

01:11:08.600 --> 01:11:09.000
Chief!

01:11:09.860 --> 01:11:12.590
Detective Goto.

01:11:13.050 --> 01:11:13.520
I'm going back to my office.

01:11:14.280 --> 01:11:16.910
What do you mean?

01:11:17.270 --> 01:11:18.450
I told you.

01:11:18.550 --> 01:11:20.030
It can't be helped if it's a genius.

01:11:20.230 --> 01:11:21.360
After you do it,

01:11:21.600 --> 01:11:23.890
If you can prove another crime, that's fine.

01:11:24.030 --> 01:11:25.260
If you can't do it,

01:11:26.540 --> 01:11:27.940
Decide on a sound blur as a disaster caused by a typhoon.

01:11:28.180 --> 01:11:29.230
If you find out, you'll find out.

01:11:29.230 --> 01:11:29.410
Thank you for watching.

01:11:30.000 --> 01:11:31.080
I'm going to have my father-in-law cut his toenails.

01:11:31.660 --> 01:11:33.380
That's Tanuki's father.

01:11:33.720 --> 01:11:35.190
I feel sorry for my father-in-law, too.

01:11:35.190 --> 01:11:36.790
I feel sorry for you, too.

01:11:36.850 --> 01:11:38.680
If that happens, we'll be criminals.

01:11:39.700 --> 01:11:41.790
Should we stop it after all?

01:11:42.460 --> 01:11:44.400
No, if you're going to regret it anyway,

01:11:44.400 --> 01:11:45.460
It's better not to do it.

01:11:46.300 --> 01:11:46.940
It's decided.

01:11:47.180 --> 01:11:53.380
I won't be back for a while.

01:11:54.060 --> 01:11:55.360
Please follow Nagumo's instructions.

01:11:55.960 --> 01:11:56.910
Roger that.

01:12:00.000 --> 01:12:01.340
Hey, what's going to happen?

01:12:01.480 --> 01:12:02.940
We're going to destroy the ship.

01:12:03.940 --> 01:12:10.360
Once the

01:12:10.360 --> 01:12:13.100
riot gang is out of the cockpit, we'll take care of it.

01:12:13.180 --> 01:12:17.700
What? But that's...

01:12:30.250 --> 01:12:30.390
This is bad!

01:12:31.360 --> 01:12:31.900
Shut up!

01:12:32.470 --> 01:12:35.290
The typhoon 19 in the northern part of the country has changed its course.

01:12:35.690 --> 01:12:38.110
Landing in the Kanto region will be unknown for a few days.

01:12:39.250 --> 01:12:40.610
It's coming!

01:12:41.150 --> 01:12:42.410
A storm is coming!

01:12:43.150 --> 01:12:47.650
It seems that we have no choice but to use the emergency system used when a fire occurs.

01:12:49.200 --> 01:12:50.740
I wonder if we can take over the central control room.

01:12:52.900 --> 01:12:54.100
The data of the guard robot.

01:13:02.110 --> 01:13:16.720
The labor setup is complete.

01:13:16.960 --> 01:13:19.150
The trailer and the float will be ready in a few hours.

01:13:19.710 --> 01:13:21.610
Anyway, how did you get that monster?

01:13:22.850 --> 01:13:25.820
I asked Kasumigaura's air force for it.

01:13:26.400 --> 01:13:28.420
I asked Kasumigaura's air force for it.

01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:32.270
I'm going to go to Narita from now on.

01:13:32.350 --> 01:13:35.060
In some cases, I'll have to deal with all the labors in Hakobune.

01:13:35.280 --> 01:13:36.760
A secret weapon...

01:13:36.760 --> 01:13:39.430
Yes, I called Masako.

01:13:39.890 --> 01:13:51.740
Sightseeing?

01:13:51.740 --> 01:13:52.060
No.

01:13:52.240 --> 01:13:52.680
Combat.

01:14:15.260 --> 01:14:26.560
There's nothing we can say now.

01:14:26.950 --> 01:14:29.700
We've received a return order. The ship is now...

01:14:30.000 --> 01:14:30.900
It's completely inhumane.

01:14:31.060 --> 01:14:32.630
Go rampage as much as you want!

01:15:05.050 --> 01:15:05.230
Are you sure?

01:15:05.750 --> 01:15:07.660
We can call them back now.

01:15:07.800 --> 01:15:10.700
Even if the plan succeeds, what if we can't prove the crime?

01:15:11.980 --> 01:15:14.150
Then we're the criminals.

01:15:14.450 --> 01:15:18.260
But if we don't do anything and the damage becomes real,

01:15:19.460 --> 01:15:20.910
we're still criminals.

01:15:21.310 --> 01:15:22.170
Which is better?

01:15:22.270 --> 01:15:26.250
Besides, we don't have a choice.

01:15:27.690 --> 01:15:29.880
If we fail...

01:15:30.000 --> 01:15:32.260
If something like this happens, the whole of Wangan will be destroyed.

01:15:32.480 --> 01:15:33.840
We don't know how far the damage will spread.

01:15:34.740 --> 01:15:40.570
But even if it succeeds, the Babylon Project will lose the white boat and make a big change.

01:15:42.050 --> 01:15:42.830
It doesn't matter which way it falls.

01:15:43.910 --> 01:15:48.750
Maybe when he jumped off, the real game was already on.

01:15:49.550 --> 01:15:51.240
Don't you think so?

01:15:51.580 --> 01:15:53.180
Are you still going to do it?

01:15:53.640 --> 01:15:55.180
Police officers have a bad personality.

01:15:55.560 --> 01:15:57.220
I'm sorry for always hurting you.

01:15:58.580 --> 01:15:59.920
Where are you going?

01:16:01.280 --> 01:16:01.900
Even though he's the head of the police,

01:16:03.160 --> 01:16:04.010
he's still in the middle of Tokyo Bay.

01:16:06.050 --> 01:16:09.890
If that's the case, the police and the police station won't be quiet.

01:16:10.630 --> 01:16:13.420
We need to get out of here and make some time.

01:16:13.680 --> 01:16:15.470
This is part of being a captain.

01:16:16.090 --> 01:16:17.490
Mr. Goto.

01:16:17.690 --> 01:16:18.030
Yes?

01:16:18.340 --> 01:16:19.670
No, it's nothing.

01:16:20.110 --> 01:16:21.140
Well then, take care of the rescue.

01:17:26.400 --> 01:17:27.320
Doesn't it feel like Yokoshima?

01:17:30.000 --> 01:17:33.740
It's a temple. It's the perfect place for a man to speak the name of Ehova.

01:17:33.800 --> 01:17:39.760
Listen! It's no big deal if you don't let the guard robots get close, but there are too many of them.

01:17:39.840 --> 01:17:43.030
Avoid fighting as much as possible. The purpose of the infiltration is to take the election.

01:17:43.150 --> 01:17:45.600
The front is open! The door is open!

01:18:00.732 --> 01:18:00.912
Oh, no.

01:18:31.400 --> 01:18:31.620
That's it!

01:19:00.540 --> 01:19:02.220
I don't know what's going to happen.

01:19:38.700 --> 01:19:39.320
It's so violent.

01:19:40.180 --> 01:19:43.650
We have to hurry or we'll be overrun by the guard robots of Hakobune.

01:19:43.970 --> 01:19:45.030
Please start the emergency.

01:19:45.950 --> 01:19:46.930
That should automatically stop the security.

01:19:48.030 --> 01:19:53.230
Let's get started.

01:19:53.670 --> 01:19:57.630
The alarm went off on the other side, too.

01:19:57.630 --> 01:19:59.940
The weather is getting better and the venue is safe.

01:20:00.000 --> 01:20:04.680
When the captain arrives at Ottori-gatama, we'll see if he's a hero or a villain.

01:20:05.440 --> 01:20:11.990
I've released the system.

01:20:12.890 --> 01:20:13.900
Roger that.

01:20:13.900 --> 01:20:15.280
Be careful.

01:20:15.740 --> 01:20:20.180
I'll ring the bell.

01:20:20.240 --> 01:20:22.020
Wait a minute.

01:20:22.560 --> 01:20:25.740
There's someone in the sub-control in the top floor.

01:20:26.460 --> 01:20:26.820
What?

01:20:30.250 --> 01:20:31.050
There's no doubt about it!

01:20:31.130 --> 01:20:32.330
Look! It's moving!

01:20:32.750 --> 01:20:45.280
It's probably dead.

01:20:46.080 --> 01:20:46.960
Could it be a ghost from the graveyard?

01:20:47.660 --> 01:20:49.240
Or is it some kind of trap?

01:20:49.500 --> 01:20:51.260
How do we communicate with it?

01:20:51.280 --> 01:20:51.950
We can't.

01:20:52.430 --> 01:20:53.990
The sub-control wasn't originally used.

01:20:55.150 --> 01:20:56.500
We have to set it up from there.

01:20:56.740 --> 01:20:58.170
We have to make sure.

01:20:59.070 --> 01:20:59.650
But there's no time!

01:21:00.600 --> 01:21:01.500
The typhoon is already landing.

